    "source_anomalies": [
      "MillionR Edition acceleration is printed as '4.2 sv'; parsed as 4.2 s (stray character).",
      "The Hill Hold row ticks only the iQube 3.1 kWh, even though the leaflet cover promotes 'Smart Hill Hold' as a headline feature. Recorded as printed - verify against TVS before using in a customer-facing build.",
      "The 2.3 kWh is the only variant with a drum front brake; all others use a 220 mm front disc.",
      "The Brakes cell prints two unlabelled values. front_brake/rear_brake reflect the real iQube layout (front disc, rear drum); brakes_as_printed keeps the source order untouched.",
      "RESOLVED: official TVS lists Rear Brake 130 mm Drum and Front Brake 220 mm Disc, confirming the front/rear assignment inferred from the leaflet.",
      "RESOLVED: MillionR acceleration is 4.2 s on the official page, confirming '4.2 sv' was a typo.",
      "Charging time disagrees between sources on three variants. Official TVS figures are used; leaflet values kept in charging_time_0_80_minutes_leaflet. 3.5 kWh and MillionR: leaflet 4h40m vs official 4h30m. ST 5.3: leaflet 4h30m vs official 4h18m.",
      "Cluster size: leaflet says 12.77 cm for 3.5 kWh and MillionR, official says 12.7 cm. Both retained.",
      "ST 5.3 certified battery capacity: leaflet says 4.8 kWh, official page says N/A. Leaflet value retained in certified_capacity_kwh.",
      "UNRESOLVED - Hill Hold. Leaflet ticks only the 3.1 kWh. BikeWale lists Hill Assist on 3.1, S 4.7 and ST 5.3. The official TVS comparison page does not list the feature at all. Treat hill_hold as unverified.",
      "Kerb weight differs between sources (BikeWale says 115 kg for the 2.3 kWh, official says 109 kg). Official used throughout."
    ],
